{
  "id": "sum-of-two-integers",
  "questionId": "sum-of-two-integers",
  "slug": "sum-of-two-integers",
  "title": "Sum of Two Integers",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Bit manipulation",
  "patterns": [
    "bit manipulation"
  ],
  "lists": [
    "blind-75"
  ],
  "hints": [
    "think about how you add two binary numbers by hand, digit by digit, tracking a carry - which single bitwise operation gives you the 'sum ignoring carry' at each position?",
    "XOR of two bits gives you exactly the sum digit ignoring any carry-in (1+0=1, 0+1=1, 1+1=0 with a carry, 0+0=0)",
    "AND of two bits tells you where a carry is generated, and that carry needs to be applied one position to the left (shifted left by 1) to be added in at the next digit",
    "repeat: compute partial_sum = a XOR b and carry = (a AND b) << 1, then set a = partial_sum and b = carry, and loop until carry becomes 0 - at that point a holds the final sum"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "not looping until carry is fully zero - a single XOR/AND pass only handles one 'layer' of carries, multi-bit carries need repeated passes",
    "in languages with fixed-width signed integers, not handling negative numbers correctly since the carry logic still relies on two's complement bit patterns working out",
    "accidentally using + or - somewhere in the implementation (even in a loop counter) when the point is to avoid them entirely for the arithmetic itself"
  ],
